      "reasoning": "All 14 answers agree with their own captured worked solutions. q-237019: zero scalar projection requires p·q=15−3x=0, so x=5. q-42157: R2←R2+4R1 produces [0,0,−2], an inconsistent equation, so there is no solution. q-73743: divide R1 by 3 and subtract 6R1 from R2 to obtain the stated echelon matrix. q-158592: (−6)sin(−π/4)=3√2. q-158574: 3ln(e²)−1=5. q-158559: the denominator square root must be positive, requiring x>−2. q-158563: require y≥−2 and y≠2x³. q-158438 and q-158569: both exponential functions are defined throughout the real plane. q-158198: x²−y²≥0 means −|x|≤y≤|x|, giving the lateral wedges with solid boundaries, option 1. q-158200: exclude only x=2, giving both sides shaded with a dashed boundary, option 1. q-98300: option 4 has no self-intersection. q-97916: option 1 crosses itself and is not simple. q-97926: option 1 has distinct endpoints and is not closed. The source illustrations for the last two questions are differently sized versions of the corresponding current curves; their mathematical properties and shapes agree. The labeled source domain illustrations also agree with their unlabeled current choices.",
